aballo  and Shawn Mendes did you know while  you're writing it that that song was  gonna be that big of a hit well when I  found out that they were involved in it  yes because you know they're two of the  biggest artists in the world and yeah I  co-wrote I mean that they are both great  writers as well actually and they had a  hand in making this song that's you know  but yeah I kind of when I heard it was  gonna come out I was like cool I was  like cool I can do some weird stuff with  my career now I can just do whatever I  want which is great I kind of give a bit  of freedom then definitely what you can  do  oh sure yeah yeah do you have for eight  songs they become huge hits and then  you're like oh I wish I saying that one  um no I think for me singing senorita  would be a bit of a fail obviously yeah  it's just you know it's not my it's not  it's not I couldn't carry it yeah I  couldn't pull it off the way they do and  obviously I'm I don't have that like  crazy high profile chemistry popstar  relationship that they do so yeah I  don't think it would have been as  successful but yeah there are songs I've  written in the past one in particular  actually one called the same old love  which I wrote with Selena Gomez which I  was like that was the closest where I  was like should I keep this but actually  the second that I heard her version I  was like no pretty neat belongs with you  and it felt really real um you are a  songwriter you're an artist you're  businesswoman you are a role model to so  many of your fans how did that feel  feels stressful like you they feel like  a pressure on well yeah  because I didn't get into music to  become a role model but obviously I  understand that it comes with the  territory  and you know I think that wherever  possible I always try and encourage my  fans or people who follow me to be  themselves just as I am you know I am  myself and I'm a human who makes  mistakes and I think that's one thing I  you know hope that they take away from  me as an artist as that humans make  mistakes and that's ok and I think there  needs to be yeah a level of life  forgiveness and in life that I feel like  sometimes doesn't really exist anymore  how would you describe your life right  now jet-lagged oh yeah that's how I  would describe it I was in Australia  like three days ago and then yesterday I  was in the UK yeah and today I'm here  and tomorrow I'm gonna be in the UK  again okay so how do you maintain your  level of energy because you perform so  you're you know you're on coffee coffee  and just adrenaline and I don't really  know I don't really know  do you ever crash after where you're  like I need no one to talk to me for a  week um you know what I somehow managed  to level out a little bit and and and  it'd be okay  so generally I find if I take too much  like time off I go a little bit crazy

